The first bracket telescopes:  $$ \begin{aligned}
\sum^{n}_{k=1} x_k^2 =& \sum^{n}_{k=1} x_k^2 +x_k-x_k
=& \sum^{n}_{k=1} x_{k+1}-x_k
=& x_{n+1}-x_1
\end{aligned} $$  The third bracket also telescopes:  $$ \begin{aligned}
\prod^{n}_{k=1} x_k+1 =& \prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k^2+x_k}{x_k}
=& \prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_{k+1}}{x_k}
=& \frac{x_{n+1}}{x_1}
\end{aligned} $$  The fourth bracket also telescopes:  $$ \begin{aligned}
\prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac1{x_k}-\frac1{x_{k+1}}=&\prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_{k+1}-x_k}{x_kx_{k+1}}
=&\prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k^2+x_k-x_k}{x_k^3+x_k^2}
=&\prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_k^2+x_k}
=&\prod^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}}
=& \frac{x_1}{x_{n+1}}
\end{aligned} $$  So the statement to be proven simplifies to:  $$ \begin{aligned}
(x_{n+1}-x_1)\left(\sum^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}}  \right)+2&=\frac{x_{n+1}}{x_1}+\frac{x_1}{x_{n+1}}
(x_{n+1}-x_1)\left(\sum^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}}  \right)&=\frac{x_{n+1}^2+x_1^2}{x_1x_{n+1}}-2
(x_{n+1}-x_1)\left(\sum^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}}  \right)&=\frac{x_{n+1}^2-2x_1x_{n+1}+x_1^2}{x_1x_{n+1}}
(x_{n+1}-x_1)\left(\sum^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}}  \right)&=\frac{x_{n+1}^2-2x_1x_{n+1}+x_1^2}{x_1x_{n+1}}
(x_{n+1}-x_1)\left(\sum^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}} \right)&=\frac{(x_{n+1}-x_1)^2}{x_1x_{n+1}}
\left(\sum^{n}_{k=1} \frac{x_k}{x_{k+1}}  \right)&=\frac{x_{n+1}-x_1}{x_1x_{n+1}}
\end{aligned} $$  Now we will prove this by induction:

First we prove the base case for  $n=1$ :  $$ \frac{x_1}{x_2}=\frac{x_2-x_1}{x_1x_2}=\frac{x_1^2+x_1-x_1}{x_1x_2}=\frac{x_1^2}{x_1x_2}=\frac{x_1}{x_2} $$  Hence the base case is proven.

For the inductive case, it suffices to prove that:   $$ \frac{x_{n+2}-x_1}{x_1x_{n+2}}-\frac{x_{n+1}-x_1}{x_1x_{n+1}}=\frac{x_{n+1}}{x_{n+2}} $$  From the LHS:  $$ \begin{aligned}
\frac{x_{n+2}-x_1}{x_1x_{n+2}}-\frac{x_{n+1}-x_1}{x_1x_{n+1}}=& \frac{x_{n+1}x_{n+2}-x_1x_{n+1}-x_{n+1}x_{n+2}+x_1x_{n+2}}{x_1x_{n+1}x_{n+2}}
=& \frac{x_1x_{n+2}-x_1x_{n+1}}{x_1x_{n+1}x_{n+2}}
=& \frac{x_{n+2}-x_{n+1}}{x_{n+1}x_{n+2}}
=& \frac{x_{n+1}^2+x_{n+1}-x_{n+1}}{x_{n+1}x_{n+2}}
=& \frac{x_{n+1}^2}{x_{n+1}x_{n+2}}
=& \frac{x_{n+1}}{x_{n+2}}
=& RHS
\end{aligned} $$  Hence the statement is proven. QED.

